{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) issued stitch task #5445 to implement srd067-split R2.1-R2.4 requirements in `cmd/split`. This involves adding byte-based splitting (`-b`/`--bytes`), line-bytes splitting (`-C`/`--line-bytes`), chunk-based splitting (`-n`/`--number` with N, l/N, r/N forms), and conflict detection between splitting modes. The existing R1.1-R1.4 implementation (line-based splitting) must not be rewritten. Differential tests covering all new functionality must be added. Acceptance criteria require: compilation without errors, all tests passing, `go vet` clean, and each of R2.1-R2.4 covered by at least one test case.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` against `gsplit` (Homebrew GNU reference binary)\n   - Size suffix parsing via `pkg/sizeparse.Parse()` (K, M, G for 1024-powers; KB, MB for 1000-powers)\n   - Line-boundary-respecting byte splitting (lines longer than N get their own piece)\n   - Chunk splitting in three forms: N (equal bytes), l/N (equal lines), r/N (round-robin lines)\n   - Mode conflict detection (only one split mode at a time)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for differential tests\n   - Alphabetic suffix generation for output files\n   - Go execution constitution: 40-line function limit, copyright headers, no git commands\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd067-split.yaml`\n     - Full SRD defining all requirements R1-R4 for the split utility\n     - R2.1: `-b N`/`--bytes=N` with size suffixes\n     - R2.2: `-C N`/`--line-bytes=N` line-boundary byte splitting\n     - R2.3: `-n CHUNKS`/`--number=CHUNKS` with N, l/N, r/N forms\n     - R2.4: Conflicting options must error exit 1\n     - package_contract imports: `pkg/sizeparse`, `pkg/sys`\n   \n   - `cmd/split/main.go` (existing, 230 lines)\n     - Current `options` struct has only `lines int` and `prefix string`\n     - `parseArgs` supports only `-l`/`--lines` flags\n     - `splitLines(r io.Reader, prefix string, linesPerPiece int)` handles line splitting\n     - `openPiece(prefix string, index int)` creates output files\n     - `alphabeticSuffix(index, length int)` generates aa, ab, ac suffixes\n     - `extractFlagValue` helper for short flag value extraction\n     - `parseLineCount` validates positive integer line counts\n     - Needs modification to add byte/chunk modes, flag parsing, and conflict detection\n   \n   - `cmd/split/split_test.go` (existing, 90 lines)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gsplit\")`\n     - `TestDiff` runs all tests via `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n     - `lineSplitTests()` covers default 1000-line, custom line count, `--lines=` form\n     - `prefixAndStdinTests()` covers custom prefix and explicit stdin dash\n     - `generateLines(from, to int) []byte` helper generates numbered lines\n     - Needs new test functions for byte, line-bytes, chunk, and conflict tests\n\n   - `pkg/sizeparse` contract (from package_contracts):\n     ```go\n     func Parse(s string) (int64, error)\n     func ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)\n     type ParseOptions struct { AllowSign bool; DefaultUnit int64 }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils` contract (from package_contracts):\n     ```go\n     type DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }\n     func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reading was performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD, existing implementation, and existing tests to understand the current state and what needs to be added. The existing code is line-split only. The implementation plan involves:\n     1. Extending `options` struct with `bytes int64`, `lineBytes int64`, `chunks string`, and a mode indicator\n     2. Adding flag parsing for `-b`, `-C`, `-n` and their long forms\n     3. Implementing `splitBytes`, `splitLineBytes`, `splitChunks` functions\n     4. Adding mode conflict detection in `parseArgs`\n     5. Adding differential test cases for each R2 requirement\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Single large message: The cobbler orchestrator task prompt containing the full task specification for stitch task #5445, including role definition, repository files list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements R1-R4, design decisions D1-D3, acceptance criteria AC1-AC4, shared protocols, and package contracts. The task is to implement srd067-split R2.1-R2.4 in `cmd/split/main.go` and add differential tests in `cmd/split/split_test.go`.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement R2.1: Add `-b N`/`--bytes=N` byte splitting with size suffix support via `pkg/sizeparse`\n   - Implement R2.2: Add `-C N`/`--line-bytes=N` line-boundary-respecting byte splitting\n   - Implement R2.3: Add `-n CHUNKS`/`--number=CHUNKS` with N, l/N, r/N chunk splitting forms\n   - Implement R2.4: Add conflict detection between splitting modes (error exit 1)\n   - Add differential test cases covering all four requirements\n   - Run `go build -o bin/split ./cmd/split/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/split/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/split/...` to verify no issues\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (`srd067-split.yaml`, `cmd/split/main.go`, `cmd/split/split_test.go`) and was about to begin implementation. I had not yet written any code or made any modifications. The next step was to plan the full implementation and then write all changes to both files before building and testing.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the R2.1-R2.4 requirements by modifying `cmd/split/main.go` to add:\n   - A split mode type/enum to track active mode (lines, bytes, lineBytes, chunks)\n   - Extended `options` struct with `bytes int64`, `lineBytes int64`, `chunks string`\n   - New flag parsing for `-b`/`--bytes`, `-C`/`--line-bytes`, `-n`/`--number` in both `parseLongFlag` and `parseShortFlags`\n   - Mode conflict detection that errors when multiple split modes are specified\n   - `splitBytes` function for R2.1\n   - `splitLineBytes` function for R2.2\n   - `splitChunks` function for R2.3 (with N, l/N, r/N sub-modes)\n   - Import `pkg/sizeparse` for size suffix parsing\n   \n   Then modify `cmd/split/split_test.go` to add test functions covering byte splitting, line-bytes splitting, chunk splitting, and conflict error cases.\n\n   The task description states: \"Extend the existing cmd/split implementation -- R1.1-R1.4 are already implemented. Do not rewrite existing code; add only the logic needed for R2.1-R2.4.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5445/431212cc-5f46-430d-83fa-488d00daeb00.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"431212cc-5f46-430d-83fa-488d00daeb00","uuid":"617fda69-08ad-41c2-a37c-8e66ed257496","timesta